<title>EGYPT: YIELD RISES ON EGYPTIAN 182-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELD RISES ON EGYPTIAN 182-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 8.820 percent at Monday's auction from 8.818 percent at the previous auction on July 14.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 992.975 million pounds, replace bills worth 903.675 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 900 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Jan 27, 1998 (Jan 13, 1998)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.820 percent (8.818)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 992.975 million (774.950 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,242.975 million (1,028.800 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.450-8.994 percent (8.480-8.899)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.450-10.200 percent (8.480-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 105 (69)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 110 (87)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
</text>
